<!-- Modal -->
<div class="modal fade" id="responseModal" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="responseModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <h5 class="modal-title" id="responseModalLabel">Tabilet API Responses</h5>
        <button type="button" class="close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close">
          <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">

<h5>Synonyms in JSON Examples</h5>
<ul><li><strong>CODE</strong>: an integer number
	<li><strong>STRING</strong>: a string
	<li><strong>HASH</strong>: a object in which the key is a string and the value a basic JSON element i.e. number, bool or string.
	<li><strong>ARRAY OF HASH</strong>: an array having <samp>HASH</samp> elements.
	<li><strong>HASH OF DATA</strong>: a object in which the key is a string but the value <samp>ARRAY OF HASH</samp>.
</ul>

<h5>Responses with HTTP Status 200</h5>
A JSON rawe string will be received, using boolean variable <em>success</em>
to indicate a possible application error.
<p></p>
<ul>
	<li>Data returned:<p>
<code class="language-json">{"success":true, "incomings":HASH, "data":ARRAY OF HASH, "included":HASH OF DATA}
</code>
</p></li>
	<li>Error returned:<p>
<code class="language-json">{"success":false, "error_code":CODE, "error_string":STRING}
</code>
</p></li>
</ul>

      </div>
      <div class="modal-footer">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

